    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Add a global (track) filter segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Required filter resource URI: vimo://<id> / local://<path>\r\n          --track TEXT        Target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 3s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --intensity TEXT    Filter intensity with normalized scalar or percent (default 60%).\r\n                              Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is invalid. Range\r\n                              after normalization: [0,1].\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: this adds a global filter on an adjustment track.\r\n      For a per-segment filter use `draft video filter add`.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add a global filter track at 80% intensity\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft filter add --resource vimo://123 --intensity 80%\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Add a global (track) filter segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Required filter resource URI: vimo://<id> / local://<path>\r\n          --track TEXT        Target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 3s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --intensity TEXT    Filter intensity with normalized scalar or percent (default 60%).\r\n                              Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is invalid. Range\r\n                              after normalization: [0,1].\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: this adds a global filter on an adjustment track.\r\n      For a per-segment filter use `draft video filter add`.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add a global filter track at 80% intensity\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft filter add --resource vimo://123 --intensity 80%\r\n",
